            <ArticleTitle>[Ambulatory pain therapy in penetrating rectal cancer via epidural anesthesia].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>88-90</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1055/s-0029-1243381</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Treatment of cancer pain includes invasive techniques of pain therapy if necessary. Here we report the management of a 55-year-old female patient with penetrating rectal cancer using continuous lumbal epidural anesthesia. After placement and dose-finding our patient was discharged from hospital and further treatment occurred at home.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Georg Thieme Verlag Stuttgart * New York.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
